<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Benjamin Constant</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1767">1767</a>–<a href="/years/1830">1830</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Benjamin Constant was a Swiss-born French political thinker of the late eighteenth and early nineteenth centuries and a leading liberal theorist. His idea of a neutral &quot;moderating power&quot; held by the monarch above the other branches of government influenced the constitution of 1824 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>. It provided the theoretical basis for the emperor's authority in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/benjamin-constant.jpg" alt="Benjamin Constant" width="320" height="391" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hercule de Roche · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roche_-_Portrait_de_Benjamin_Constant_(1767-1830),_%C3%A9crivain_et_homme_politique_-_P1679_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Carnavalet_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The system derived from the constitutional theory of the French-Swiss writer <b>Benjamin Constant</b>, and it gave Pedro II considerable authority exercised through constitutional forms.</blockquote><a href="/empire/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>Among them <b>Benjamin Constant</b>, one of the first thinkers to go by the name of liberal, set the participatory “Liberty of the Ancients” against the “Liberty of the Moderns”, founded on civil liberties, the rule of law and elected representatives.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/liberalism">Liberalism · Spread &amp; Variants</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lausanne">Lausanne</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/switzerland">Switzerland</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=46.53,6.63&amp;year=1807" aria-label="Lausanne on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4706 528 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Benjamin Constant"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5156 798h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5156 798h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=46.53,6.63&amp;year=1807">What was here in 1807? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
